{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>From all your gifts you shall lift up.</b> This teaches that even from grain grown in the field of the pasture-lands of Levite cities they are obligated to give to the priests — lest the Levite say: from grain grown within my own property I am not obligated to separate; a fortiori, from others' property I benefit, from my own all the more so! Therefore it says <b>from all your gifts.</b> And we find that the field of the pasture-land is called a gift, as it is written: ״ומגרש לערים סביבותיהם תתנו ללויים״ (and you shall give pasture-land around their cities to the Levites)." "<b>From all its fat, its holy portion from it.</b> From the best and from the finest of it you shall separate from it. <b>Its holy portion</b> — that is, the terumah."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:34.554009766Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}